# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and *then* `COPY . .`, so without this file a
# local `docker build` copies the host's node_modules over the container's.
# esbuild and rollup ship platform-specific binaries (@esbuild/win32-x64,
# @rollup/rollup-win32-x64-*), so a Windows or macOS host silently replaces the
# Linux ones and `npm run build` fails inside the image.
#
# It also keeps the local SQLite database out: the image must boot with an empty
# volume so scripts/seed-if-empty.ts publishes on first run, rather than
# shipping whatever happened to be in data/ on someone's laptop.
#
# Deliberately conservative — everything the build or the runtime touches stays.
# configs/ is required at runtime (seeding and the admin publish page), and
# scripts/ holds the first-boot seed the CMD invokes.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`.
dist

# Local database; the deployed one lives on the mounted volume at /data.
data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store

# Not part of the running service.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
deploy
*.pdf
